                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^k
              for the
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              = succeed ".)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            %p
              This is the value of a function at
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              with is the sum over the product of two smooth functions, namely the component functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi i
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (v_i)^k
              of the smooth section in the given chart, and the derivatives of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i
              (which are functions by the assumption that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is smooth).
            %p
              This shows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_v(f)
              is a smooth function.
            %p
              Now for the converse. Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Der
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \in Der(\C^\infty(X))
              be a derivation, we need to show that it arises on each chart
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_i
              from smooth vector field
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_i
              as above.
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hadamard+lemma"} Hadamard lemma
              gives that every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i \colon \mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R}^1
              may be written for each point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \mathbb{R}^n
              as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo −
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi y
                      %mi k
                    %mo −
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f(y) = f(y-x) + \sum_{k = 0}^n (y^k - x^k) \cdot g_{x,k}(y)
            %p for smooth functions
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{g_k \in C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)\}_{k \in \{1,\cdots, n\}}
            %p satisfying
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %msup
                          %mi y
                          %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo =
                        %mi x
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    g_{x,k}(x) = \frac{\partial f(y)}{\partial y^k}\vert_{y = x}
                    \\,.
            %p Now by the derivation property we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi D
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 0
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo +
                              %munderover
                                %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                                %mrow
                                  %mi k
                                  %mo =
                                  %mn 1
                                %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mi k
                              %mo −
                              %msup
                                %mi x
                                %mi k
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ⋅
                              %msub
                                %mi g
                                %mrow
                                  %mi x
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mi k
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %munderover
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mrow
                                %mi k
                                %mo =
                                %mn 1
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi D
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mi k
                              %mo −
                              %msup
                                %mi x
                                %mi k
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⋅
                            %msub
                              %mi g
                              %mrow
                                %mi x
                                %mo ,
                                %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi k
                            %mo −
                            %msup
                              %mi x
                              %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mi D
                            %msub
                              %mi g
                              %mrow
                                %mi x
                                %mo ,
                                %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %munderover
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mrow
                                %mi k
                                %mo =
                                %mn 1
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mi i
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mfrac
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∂
                                %mi f
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi y
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∂
                                %msup
                                  %mi y
                                  %mi k
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mrow
                                %mi y
                                %mo =
                                %mi x
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    D(f)(x)
                    \&amp; =
                    D
                    \\left(
                    f(0)
                    +
                    \\sum_{k = 1}^n  ((-)^k - x^k) \cdot g_{x,k}(-)
                    \\right)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\sum_{k = 1}^n
                    \\big(
                    {(D( (-)^k - x^k ))} \cdot g_{x,k}(-)
                    +
                    ((-)^k - x^k) \cdot D g_{x,k}(-)
                    \\big)(x)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\sum_{k = 1}^n (v_i)^k(x) \cdot \frac{\partial f(y)}{\partial y^k}\vert_{y = x}
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Here in the last step we
              %em defined
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi i
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (v_i)^k(x) \coloneqq D( (-)^k )(x)
            %p
              to be the value at
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              of the function which the derivation produces when applied to the
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              by definition of
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_{x,k}
              as well as that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi k
                    %mo −
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^k - x^k
              vanishes at
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %p
              This shows that the derivation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              comes, in the chart
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_i
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_i
              as above.
